==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
*1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A strategy to beat this level is to spam [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] and any other meatshields just before the boss is released. Try to build up a high amount of long-ranged attackers such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. Make sure you keep meatshielding, otherwise J.K. Bun Bun will kill all of your attackers.

[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] is very helpful in this stage. It can do massive damage each shot and it can also slow Red enemies. You could also do with some [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] or [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] cats like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] and so on. You could also stack [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] in order to pin J.K. Bun Bun to the base. The abundance of Floating enemies allows [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] to thrive in this stage. Additionally, crowd-controllers like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] works wonders in crowd controlling Bun Bun.

There is no reason to be scared of the Mooths, as they are only at 100% strength magnification and are really easy to beat. Use the Mooths as money bags, as they have enough to buy a Bahamut.

This stage can be easily beaten with just many meatshields and some ranged attackers, not unlike in [[Teacher Bun Bun]]'s [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|debut stage]].

